Z||000000||WMEBERT||05-18-2001||09:16 AM||||I'm returning to the Fiero fold after a 16 year absence.  My 1st was a white SE I bought new in '84 after I re-upped in Uncle Sam's Army to get a big bonus to buy it! Now my brother-in-laws '86 GT developed a water leak from a 2 year old Parts America rebuild and he's tired of dealing with it.  It's mine for a grand...couldn't pass it up at that price.  My question is "How much does it weigh"  I'll need to tow dolly it home on about 8 miles of flat road and I only have a Class II hitch on my S10 Blazer-3500 pound tow capacity.  I'm hoping I'll be okay-let me know.<P>I'll be at Carlisle on Saturday getting goodies for it!  Praying for sun!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||RacinRob||05-18-2001||10:04 AM||||did you look for the door sticker? that might be more accurate.  but it is between 2600 and 2900 LBS.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WMEBERT||05-18-2001||10:32 AM||||Thanks for the reply RacinRob.  I haven't been over to check the door sticker-hadn't really thought of it to be honest.  I was pretty sure it was lighter then the 3500 pounds my hitch is rated for. Looking forward to getting it home and getting it running.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Butter||05-18-2001||10:50 AM||||WMEBERT,<BR>My 84 2m8 clocks in at 2750lbs on COOP scales.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gt2437||05-18-2001||11:03 AM||||All (stock) Fiero's weigh between 2450 and 2750 lbs IIRC.  Duke's and less optioned models being on light end and GT's (& formulas)being on the higher end of that scale.<P>[edit] i think it's even narrower between 2500 and 2700  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> [edit]<p>[This message has been edited by gt2437 (edited 05-18-2001).]||||reg||1
